1
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:09,000
The film. The classic musical comes to the big screen for the first time.

2
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
The Phantom of the Opera is a thriller, drama,
romance film directed by Joel Schumacher.

3
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:15,000
A young soprano becomes the obsession of a disfigured and murderous
musical genius who lives beneath the Paris Opera House.

4
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
The Phantom, played by Gerard Butler.

5
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Christine, played by Emmy Rossum.

6
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Raoul, played by Patrick Wilson.

7
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:27,000
Madame Giry, played by Miranda Richardson.

8
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Carlotta, played by Minnie Driver.

9
01:03:27,000 --> 01:03:33,000
Firmin, played by Ciarán Hinds.

10
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
The Phantom of the Opera is a 2004 musical romantic drama film based on Andrew Lloyd Webber's musical of
the same name, which in turn is based on Gaston Leroux's novel, Le Fantôme de l'Opéra.

11
01:17:33,000 --> 01:17:39,000
Produced and co-written by Lloyd Webber and directed by Joel Schumacher, the film features an ensemble cast consisting of Gerard Butler as the titular character, with
Emmy Rossum, Patrick Wilson, Miranda Richardson, Minnie Driver, Simon Callow, Ciarán Hinds, Victor McGuire and Jennifer Ellison in supporting roles.

12
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
The film was announced in 1989, although production did not start until 2002
due to Lloyd Webber's divorce and Schumacher's busy career.

13
01:31:39,000 --> 01:31:45,000
It was shot entirely at Pinewood Studios, with scenery
created with miniatures and computer graphics.

14
01:38:42,000 --> 01:38:48,000
Rossum, Wilson and Driver had singing experience, but Butler had none
and was provided with music lessons prior to filming.

15
01:45:45,000 --> 01:45:51,000
The Phantom of the Opera grossed $154.6 million worldwide.

16
01:52:48,000 --> 01:52:54,000
It received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for the visuals and acting, particularly the performances of the lead
actors, but criticism towards the writing, direction and unnecessary deviations from the source material.

17
01:59:51,000 --> 01:59:57,000
Despite its initial reception, the film received several awards and a trio of
Oscar nominations, as well as a positive reception from the audience.

18
02:06:54,000 --> 02:07:00,000
The film explores themes of mask, dancing, paris, france,
based on novel or book, love triangle.

19
02:13:57,000 --> 02:14:03,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
